<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saco, Maine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saco is a city in southern Maine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, on the Saco River near its mouth, opposite Biddeford. English fishermen and settlers arrived in the 1620s and 1630s, and it formed part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinando-gorges">Sir Ferdinando Gorges</a>'s Province of Maine before Massachusetts absorbed the region in the 1650s. In the 19th century it grew as a textile mill town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saco-maine.jpg" alt="Saco, Maine" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kenneth C. Zirkel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Main_Street,_Saco_Maine.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
